{title: Come Down O Love Divine}
{key: C}
{time: 2/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Come [C]down, O [G]Love [F]di[C]vine, seek [**]thou this [Am]soul [D]of [G]mine
And [F]visit it with [Dm]thine own ardor [G]glo[C]wing
O [Am]Comfor[C]ter, draw [G]near, [Bb]with[F]in my [Dm]heart [C]ap[G]pear
And [C]kindle [G]it, thy [C]holy [Dm]flame be[G]stow[C]ing.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O [C]let it [G]free[F]ly [C]burn, till [**]earthly [Am]pas[D]sions [G]turn
To [F]dust and ashes [Dm]in its heat con[G]su[C]ming
And [Am]let thy [C]glo[D]rious [G]light [Bb]shine [F]ever [Dm]on [C]my [G]sight
And [C]clothe me [G]round, the [C]while my [Dm]path il[G]lu[C]ming.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And [C]so the [G]year[F]ning [C]strong, with [**]which the [Am]soul [D]will [G]long
Shall [F]far outpass the [Dm]power of human [G]tell[C]ing
For [Am]none can [C]guess [D]its [G]grace, till [F]we be[Dm]come [C]the [G]place
[G]Where[C]in the [G]Holy [C]Spirit [Dm]makes a [G]dwell[C]ing.
{end_of_verse}
